The final update is out!

Hi everyone,

The final update for PROZE: Prologue is available now. It further polishes the game and adds new content – delivering the experience we were always aiming for.

What’s new: 

An expanded story with new puzzles and interactions;
Updated animations and 3D-models;
Interactive music;
New dialogues and voiceover;
Tuned interactions mechanics;
Further performance optimization.

With these additions, we are now confident in PROZE: Prologue quality. So now it’s time to focus on the Episode I production. It comes out in February, and we’re excited to share the first details when the time comes.

Meanwhile, enjoy the Prologue in its full!

https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/steamcommunity/public/images/clans/33360089/601d84a2203074a18f4f7b05d2b461ac2e4db5c9.jpg
A new update is now available for PROZE: Prologue. The free opening chapter for PROZE now features two new puzzles, as well as performance and graphics optimization.

Besides new content, the update adds as many VR customization options as possible, so you can play the game as you feel comfortable – sitting or standing, with character body or without, turning with movement or with controller input, etc.

New features:

-performance optimization;
-improved 3D models, more visual details;
-new interactive objects;
-more detailed sound effects;
-two new puzzles;
-movement improvements:
VIVE – touch to move, turning options, tuned movement speed;
Oculus Rift – movement with left touch controller option;
new input and gameplay options: body display, vignette display, sitting and standing positions, locomotion turning.

Please tell us what you think!

https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/steamcommunity/public/images/clans/33360089/625cd78c8f38b5225ca18591f6e3625ad8cd7632.jpg Thanks for playing and sharing your comments and impressions! We’ve listened to your feedback and prepared a first major patch for PROZE: Prologue – available now.

What’s new:

– performance optimization;
– Vive controllers improvements;
– fixed texture streaming;
– body positioning improvements (Oculus only this time, we’re working on a Vive fix too);
– vignette turn off option added.

Share your thoughts with us! We’re aiming to bring the best possible VR experience in PROZE.
